          %p
            The
            %em Cayley-Dickson construction
            or
            %em Cayley-Dickson double
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dickson1919"}> Dickson 1919, (6)
            ) takes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to a new real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            whose elements are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            of elements of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            arise as a doubling of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %p
            When iteratively applied to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} trivial
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            (thus all four
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+normed+division+algebras"} real normed division algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sedenions"} sedenions
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonassociative+algebra"} possibly nonassociative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline(-) \colon x \mapsto \overline{x}
            which is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antiautomorphism"} antiautomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            could be replaced by any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            in the definitions, although some properties may depend on this ring.)
          %h3#definition_in_components Definition in components
          #CayleyDicksonDoubleInComponents.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Cayley-Dickson construction in components)
            %p
              The
              %em Cayley–Dickson double
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CD
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CD(A)
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  whose underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \oplus A
              %li
                %p whose multiplication is given by
                #eq:ProductInComponents.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mi c
                        %mo −
                        %mi d
                        %mover
                          %mi b
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi d
                        %mo +
                        %mi c
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (a,b)
                        (c, d)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        (a c - d \overline{b}, \overline{a} d + c b)
              %li
                %p
                  whose star-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                  is given by
                #eq:InvolutionInComponents.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ¯
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi a
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\widebar{(a,b)}
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        (\overline{a},-b)
                        \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dickson1919"}> Dickson 1919, (6)
            )
          %h3#DefinitionByGeneratorsAndRelations Definition by generators and relations
          #CayleyDicksonDoubleByAdjoiningFurtherGenerator.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (Cayley-Dickson double by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators and relations
            %p
              The
              %em Cayley-Dickson double
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi CD
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde{CD}(A)
              obtained by adjoining one generator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              subject to the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relations
            #eq:TheNewGenerator.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mover
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ell^2 \;=\; -1
                    \\,,
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    \\overline{\ell}
                    \\;=\;
                    \- \ell
            %p and
            #eq:DicksonRelations.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mi b
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a (\ell b)
